{"c":[{"id":"31cdacff4b10c371","sum":"Chrome web AX: nativeYields; H14 'pagetask start'. W1: guard-adversary class (a) 0; writes via writable.ts writeMisfit. Page writes need a CheckedValue (test/mint.ts). Ask scope: code only vetoes. $0 Ask replay: CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1928d54605e94465","sum":"Chrome web AX: nativeYields; publish invalidates offer. H14: pagetask start, no guest Jev, banners cover panels. Live sets once; HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false. W1: guard-adversary class(a) writes 0; labelled lines offer parts; writeMisfit owns rules; candidates added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"686710946312e7ea","sum":"Chrome ignores native AX writes once web AX is on (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its live offer first. H14 rig: no guest Jev, use 'pagetask start'; banners cover top-right panels.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"806a636804d6e5d8","sum":"Chrome page fields: once web AX is on, Chrome ignores native AX writes (HostCoordinator yields via PageInline.nativeYields); PageTaskMachine.publish invalidates its own live offer before republishing, or onDisplaced drops the page task.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T172603Z-a7ca0252d9058e55","text":"Once an assistive app turns on Chrome's web accessibility, native ghost text sees page fields, but Chrome ignores its AX writes (writeIgnored): Tab is eaten. HostCoordinator yields to page inline text via PageInline.nativeYields.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211151Z-05df8b8f447e91f6","text":"H14: PageTaskMachine.publish must invalidate its own live offer before republishing (a click changes the preview without a key): otherwise the arbiter's onDisplaced puts the whole page task away.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"cfa933fb97832a8e","sum":"H14 rig: guest has no Jev; drive attach rows with hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>' (pageTask.lastAccept* shows Tab). Banners cover top-right panels: give canned page goals a lower viewport. clickableContent panels need a mouse move before a click.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261006T211204Z-63399dc84dfcee60","text":"H14: the rig guest has no Jev, so an Ask gives no page goal; drive attach rows with test hook 'pagetask start <goalProgress>'. The helper echoes no goalAccept: state pageTask.lastAccept* shows what Tab sent.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261006T211204Z-f2f5d457e6044752","text":"H14: macOS notification banners cover Caret's panels at the screen's top right; a rig click there hits the banner. Give canned page goals a viewport lower down. clickableContent panels take a click only after a mouse move over them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ca6b56f177286a70","sum":"Live Jev: run sets once (43-81 requests/pass); HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false (LV1). W1: offline guard-adversary.ts each batch, class (a) writes 0; labelled lines offer parts. All chosen writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there; candidates added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"99b0cde49d41360f","sum":"Live Jev: run live sets once (R1's slow-eval never settles; each pass sends 43-81 new requests). Keep HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS false: on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T015102Z-70f8faec6a3a0648","text":"R1's slow-eval runner never settles on live Jev: each pass sends 43-81 new requests, so a set costs about 3x one pass. Run live sets once.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T015102Z-cf129cc10068e635","text":"HOIST_SHARED_OPTIONS changes Jev's answers: with it on, Jev answered 'none' on names and emails on four small forms. Keep it false (LV1 compare-hoist.txt).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5678229122db2693","sum":"W1: run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts offline each batch; class (a) writes must stay 0. Labelled multi-value lines offer parts, not whole lines. All chosen-value writes use fill/writable.ts writeMisfit; add rules there. Candidates are added, never swapped.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T020955Z-5dafeedfea56fda2","text":"W1: canned evals never pick a plausible wrong candidate; run helper/scripts/guard-adversary.ts (offline, ~2 s) each batch: class (a) writes must stay 0. A labelled multi-value line offers its parts, not its whole (line-values severalValues).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T025421Z-86d442b2d62eead8","text":"Any path that writes a chosen value into a field checks fill/writable.ts writeMisfit (fill, planner validate, codeplan, offer filter, goal gate); add new value rules there, not beside one caller. Candidates are only added, never swapped out.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c91d936f6921fcb","sum":"Canned page-loop evals answer owners from owners.json; page writes need a CheckedValue (test mints: test/mint.ts). Ask scope is Jev's per-field ask, code only vetoes (ask-scope-eval.ts). $0 Ask replay: CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE, nonzero --spend-limit.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f9ac8be3313a624c","sum":"G2: note lines go whole before clauses; contact clauses charge first outside chats; canned evals answer owners from owners.json. W2/I1: every page write needs a CheckedValue or compilers throw; test mints use test/mint.ts minted(p, model).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"9eb8c86cfea56fc0","sum":"G2: note short lines go whole before clauses; date/email/phone partAround clauses charge first only outside chats (earlier, canned 316->308). Canned page-loop evals answer owners from fixtures/web-form/owners.json, else unclear 0.5; a page with no entry throws.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T034441Z-339e891dadd6a49a","text":"G2: a note's short lines go out whole and spend its budget before any clause; date/email/phone clause parts (partAround) are charged before other lines only outside conversations; earlier charging cut emails and names (guard-adversary canned 316 -> 308/314).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T034441Z-3d8738b69dcb6bd3","text":"G2: canned page-loop evals answer fill's ownership questions from fixtures/web-form/owners.json (W4: ~/.caret-run/evidence/browser/w4/replay/owners.json), unclear 0.5 elsewhere; a canned run throws for a page with no entry.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"eafc5c507969e166","sum":"W2/I1: every page write needs a CheckedValue (fill/contract.ts checkValues/mintExempt) or compilers throw ContractError; provenanceStale is the one source recheck and lines [] never holds, so hand-built test mints use test/mint.ts minted(p, model).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T050339Z-4d8696f9c3182cf8","text":"W2: every page write needs a CheckedValue from helper/src/fill/contract.ts (checkValues or mintExempt); compilers (fillPlan, validatePlan, GoalRuns.propose, patterns plan) throw ContractError without one. Proposals built by hand in tests go through test/mint.ts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T091312Z-bde14560b8505461","text":"I1: the only source recheck is fill/contract.ts provenanceStale (G2's sourceHolds merged in, deleted); a window Provenance needs lines = lineDigests of the text Jev judged, and lines [] is never held, so hand-built test mints pass a model (test/mint.ts minted(p, model)).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2dc524fd37e482b","sum":"Ask scope is Jev's per-field ask; code only vetoes, never hand-written reading rules; recalibrate SCOPE_CUTOFF via ask-scope-eval.ts. $0 Ask replay: CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE, nonzero --spend-limit. Date assumptions go to the verifier with Provenance.says.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"0ac61137cde78f4e","sum":"Ask scope is Jev's per-field scope ask (asks/not/unclear, 2 wordings, SCOPE_CUTOFF); code only vetoes, never hand-written reading rules (A2's 12 rounds failed). After rewording, recalibrate with scripts/ask-scope-eval.ts (--answers rescores free).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T094325Z-2ecfd9f27d40a67e","text":"Ask scope is Jev's per-field scope ask (asks/not/unclear, two wordings, SCOPE_CUTOFF); code only vetoes. Answer a widening finding with a veto or 'unclear', never a hand-written reading rule: A2's twelve rounds of those never converged.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T094325Z-46934d63d09e671d","text":"Recalibrate SCOPE_CUTOFF after changing the scope ask's wording: scripts/ask-scope-eval.ts scores Jev's answers against scripts/ask-scope-labels.json; --answers rescores a saved run for free.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b8239301d4a3ddf5","sum":"Ask evals: a $0 replay needs CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, no CARET_ENV_FILE and a nonzero --spend-limit; fill dates: any resolver assumption goes to the verifier with Provenance.says, and send-line years and stated-format orders are their own candidates.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T103113Z-2eca6bf2c96e40c9","text":"Ask evals: realfill-asks --spend-limit 0 refuses replayed requests too; for a $0 replay set CARET_JEV_CACHE_MODE=replay, unset CARET_ENV_FILE and pass a nonzero --spend-limit (misses fail as jevFailed).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T113449Z-ded1f2a70adbf732","text":"fill dates: any resolver assumption (year from a reference, order from a format/locale, century) sends the value to the verifier with Provenance.says; send-line years and stated-format orders are offered as their own candidates; a raw span never takes them.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"60d26462cee66ea4","sum":"Undo whole-field; Ask ask.scope/answeringScope; <=8 unclear sure; formInputs web combos; secret opener next line; realfill-asks page. SC1 Disclosure/minted.ts, ModelText/shapes.ts, [withheld], KEY note_1. App builds privacy_gate.sh+PrivacyPromise.txt; release CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1","tree":{"c":[{"id":"7b6c418ead30eff1","sum":"Undo is whole-field; Asks ask ask.scope first (stand-ins need answeringScope); <=8 unclear use sure. formInputs adds web comboboxes; a secret opener takes the next line. realfill-asks defaults to page. SC1 requests carry a Disclosure; tests use test/minted.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"1642b5380f13f0bc","sum":"Undo: whole-field only. Ask: Jev ask.scope per field; stand-ins need answeringScope. Settled fields fill; <=8 unclear use sure, else unsure; no ambiguity/length refusal. AX closed selects show selection only; realfill keeps options, no legends/headings except radio groups.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"177848396eca6f4e","sum":"Helper undo covers whole-field replacements, not host/extension caret/selection/append insertions. Every Ask first asks Jev ask.scope per field; test stand-ins need answeringScope from helper/test/builders.ts or Asks refuse/ask back.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T132116Z-e94ee4791db7e513","text":"The helper executor replaces whole fields; caret/selection/append insertion runs in the host or extension and never enters the executor undo ledger.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T144012Z-e2952279328219e3","text":"Every Ask route asks Jev's per-field scope question (purpose ask.scope) first, so a test Jev stand-in must answer it: wrap it with answeringScope in helper/test/builders.ts, or Asks refuse or ask back.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0ec40e0d5ae540d2","sum":"Ask fills settled fields; <=8 unclear fields use sure, else unsure; no refusal for ambiguity/length. Chrome AX closed selects expose only the selection. realfill page walks keep options but no legends/headings except radio groups.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T144012Z-ef6cc9d6c94c61fb","text":"I3 ruling: an Ask never refuses for unclear fields or a too-long question; Jev's settled fields fill, unclear ones are asked beside them (AskIntent.sure) only when <= 8, else listed as left to the user (AskIntent.unsure).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T162248Z-4dec6eda4a1a65ff","text":"Chrome AX shows a closed select's selected option only, so realfill-asks' default reader desk has no menu options; --form-window page uses the page walks (helper/fixtures/recorded/realfill-pages), which keep no fieldset legend or heading except a radio group's.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b616cda88a55aeb3","sum":"formInputs synthesizes editable web comboboxes; a secret opener takes the whole next line; clauses respect quotes, literals from retained spans. realfill-asks defaults to page (reader for pre-V4). SC1 requests carry a Disclosure; tests wrap in test/minted.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"f2b260f724b03eed","sum":"Form reading and redaction: formInputs synthesizes editable web comboboxes (formControls alone is incomplete); a secret opener takes the whole next line; instruction clauses respect quotes and model literals come from separate retained spans.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T164500Z-f23002306114cfa8","text":"Editable web comboboxes are synthesized by formInputs; formControls alone is not a complete inventory for retaining fill inputs.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T173911Z-5d012ef86eac725c","text":"A secret opener consumes the whole next physical line, including conjunctions in its value. Instruction clauses must respect quotes, and model literals must come from separate retained spans.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"18b4fb1a390dd6dc","sum":"realfill-asks defaults to --form-window page since I4 (reader for pre-V4 compares; slow-eval pins reader). SC1: every Jev/writer request carries a Disclosure the clients verify; test requests wrap in test/minted.ts; structuredClone drops it (clone the body).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T183953Z-6f2314940641602e","text":"realfill-asks defaults to --form-window page since I4 (the helper plans browser Asks on the page walk); pass --form-window reader to compare with pre-V4 runs. slow-eval's Ask sets pin reader for their P1 references.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T194509Z-1033502c97d598d1","text":"SC1: every Jev/writer request carries a Disclosure (privacy/disclosure.ts) that the clients verify; hand-built test requests wrap in test/minted.ts, and structuredClone of a request loses its Disclosure (clone the body, keep the object).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"7bd01f8a829ee9fd","sum":"Privacy: request text is ModelText only, every slot needs a shapes.ts row, excluded values read [withheld]; Disclosure keys match KEY (note_1). Every app build runs privacy_gate.sh (acceptances, no Vercel opt-in, bundled PrivacyPromise.txt); release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"bf2aa89d755a6e5f","sum":"SC1: request text is ModelText only (derived for reformats; casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary); exclude.ts counts lower/upper/digit; excluded values read in as [withheld]. Every slot needs a shapes.ts row. Field-format mints trace to their window source.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"2925274083aef64a","sum":"SC1: exclude.ts high-entropy counts lower/upper/digit only (symbols broke B25 held-16); excluded values read in as [withheld]. Request text is ModelText only (own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText, derived for reformats); casts outside src/privacy/ fail sc1-boundary.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T200650Z-ffcd5d83b2f9fc55","text":"SC1 exclude.ts: the high-entropy rule counts only lower/upper/digit classes; counting symbols flagged corpus URL paths (51310/forms/greenhouse-apply) and broke B25 held-16. Excluded values become [withheld] at read-in; writes and memory refuse any text holding it.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T211138Z-929a7c53a65ffe04","text":"SC1: request text compiles only as ModelText (privacy/disclosure.ts own/t/descriptor/candidate/memoryText); mint a reformatted value with derived(base, text), which refuses words the screen never showed. A ModelText cast outside src/privacy/ fails test/sc1-boundary.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6af8d35d2cbd1bc9","sum":"Field-format candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and assumptions through both verifier wordings; validation traces the mint to its window source. Every request slot needs a privacy/shapes.ts row, or verify throws OutOfShape; purpose-less requests carry own() only.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261007T213034Z-ef7ccd2a17aa97dd","text":"Field-format fill candidates carry fieldFormat provenance and conversion assumptions through both verifier wordings; planner validation traces a genuine mint to its original window source and rechecks provenance, since formatted text need not occur verbatim.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261007T215427Z-85a4a1e31491fed7","text":"Every request slot needs a row in helper/src/privacy/shapes.ts: Disclosure.verify throws OutOfShape for a path with no row, a mint reason the row disallows, or text over its max; a request with no purpose may carry only own() wording.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e5f9cbd94aab9fee","sum":"All app builds run privacy_gate.sh: accepted.ts needs pv2-sites-send + ha2-copied-conversation; Vercel dev opt-in refused; onboarding shows bundled PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1. Disclosure keys match KEY (note_1); dynamic maps need a shapes.ts childGlob.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"009e4aa697218076","sum":"privacy_gate.sh runs on every build (Debug, build-app.sh, helper bundling): accepted.ts records pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation; CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 refused; onboarding renders PrivacyPromise.txt; release sets CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1 (no Vercel).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T001204Z-bb38791614f982ff","text":"Caret app builds, including Debug, run scripts/privacy_gate.sh; helper/src/privacy/accepted.ts must record lead acceptance of pv2-sites-send and ha2-copied-conversation before builds pass, and CARET_DEV_VERCEL_GEMINI=1 is refused at build time.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T002947Z-c019705c5089f866","text":"The privacy gate also covers apps/caret/scripts/build-app.sh and direct helper bundling; onboarding must render generated Contents/Resources/PrivacyPromise.txt. Release child environments set CARET_RELEASE_HOST=1, which refuses every Vercel route even with a dev opt-in.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ceaba173a4e941d3","sum":"Xcode privacy phases: first checks source plists, last needs the processed bundle plist. Release env extraction keeps only TypeSafe settings. Disclosure.walk refuses body keys with spaces (use note_1); dynamic state maps need a childGlob rule in shapes.ts.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T004510Z-16ddc03f0a00f357","text":"Xcode's first privacy phase checks source plists; its last requires the processed bundle plist as an input. Release helper env-file extraction preserves TypeSafe key/provider/model/cap and refuses other providers before spawn.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T030901Z-9525a678a3afd6cf","text":"Disclosure.walk refuses any request-body key outside KEY (no spaces), so ids like 'note 1' cannot be state keys (INT1 uses note_1); a state map with dynamic keys also needs a childGlob rule in privacy/shapes.ts besides its .* row.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
